session:pr541Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #540 asked for regression tests confirming IncrementalReasoner::apply_deletions (datalog/src/incremental.rs) correctly cascades retraction through derivation chains deeper than the existing single-hop tests exercised, following an investigation of the code against Motik et al.'s Backward/Forward paper that concluded (by reading, not testing) that backward_phase's reverse-witness BFS has no hop limit and forward_phase fully re-derives survivors. Two tests were added: a strictly linear depth-3 chain (each link a single-body-atom rule so each derived fact has exactly one witness, forcing backward_phase to walk derived-depends-on-derived hops rather than short-circuiting through a multi-witness rule), and a deep diamond where a fact has both a depth-1 and depth-4 derivation path, deleting the depth-1 support to confirm forward_phase's re-derivation keeps the fact alive via the surviving depth-4 path. Both tests passed against the existing implementation with zero production-code changes, confirming the prior code-reading conclusion rather than finding a bug -- the expected and anticipated outcome per the issue's own scoping. A related orchestration note: the implementing sub-agent stalled twice waiting on its own backgrounded cargo commands instead of blocking on them (a recurring pattern this session, since the harness auto-backgrounds anything over ~2 minutes); rather than resume it a third time, the orchestrating session verified the uncommitted diff directly, ran the full quality gate itself, and finished the PR." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:541 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr541 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .
